    Bug 1890253 - Unified fix for POP3 filter moves and duplicate cleanup. r=BenC,mkmelin


    This patch stabilizes the legacy POP3 delivery engine by unifying local move
    and delete operations under a single, architecturally sound pipeline.

    1. Fixes "Zombie" messages, mbox bloat, and Virtual Folder deduplication (Bug 1890253):
       Replaces the broken DiscardNewMessage/RemoveHeaderMdbRow sequence in
       MoveIncorporatedMessage with a targeted msgStore->DeleteStoreMessages and a silent
       sourceDB->DeleteHeader. By bypassing the high-level folder deletion API, this
       prevents local filter moves from incorrectly mirroring deletions to the POP3
       server (ignoring "Leave on server" prefs) and stops Virtual Folders from
       miscalculating unread counts via cross-wired notification events.

    2. Fixes Maildir move failures (Bug 1767190):
       Removes the brittle MoveNewlyDownloadedMessage fast-path from the IDL
       and nsParseNewMailState. This forces both mbox and maildir to use the
       stream-based fallback, bypassing the OS-level file lock collisions
       (Windows 0x8055000F, Linux 0x80520005) that occurred during filter moves.
       Additionally, explicitly releases the input stream handle before deletion
       to prevent Windows sharing violations.

    3. Cleans up Duplicate Detection and Enforces Atomicity (Bug 1951049):
       Updates 'deleteDups' and 'moveDupsToTrash' to utilize the new HardDeleteDetachedMessage
       utility (AttachHdr -> msgStore->DeleteStoreMessages -> sourceDB->DeleteHeader).
       This strict pipeline guarantees atomicity by aborting the database deletion if
       the physical store wipe fails, ensuring the DB and physical disk stay in sync.
       It also logs silent source-deletion failures to the JS Error Console.

    4. Architectural Refactor & Panorama Compatibility:
       Extracts HardDeleteDetachedMessage and AppendMsgFromStream into pure,
       file-local utilities to reduce state coupling. AppendMsgFromStream now
       explicitly updates SetMessageSize using the exact bytes copied to disk,
       preventing historical UI/DB size desyncs.
       Removes the redundant removeHeaderMdbRow from nsIMsgDatabase. Utilizes
       AttachHdr for SQLite compatibility, and explicitly updates the
       m_msgToForwardOrReply pointer in PublishMsgHeader to prevent
       auto-forwarding failures on detached headers.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D287786

